# Accessibility rules (WCAG 2.1 / 2.2 Level AA)

## Doc map

- **Setup & commands** → [README.md](../../README.md)
- **System design & deployment** → [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)
- **Stack, paths & conventions** → [PROJECT.md](../../PROJECT.md)

**Principle:** Accessibility before responsive polish. Labels, keyboard operability, and focus order are non-negotiable.

## Perceivable

- Every `<img>` needs meaningful `alt` or `alt=""` when decorative.
- Icons without visible text need `aria-label` or visually hidden text.
- Contrast: ≥ 4.5:1 normal text, ≥ 3:1 large text and UI/focus indicators.
- Never convey meaning by color alone.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for non-essential animation.
- Usable at 200% zoom without horizontal scroll on primary content.

## Operable

- All interactive elements keyboard reachable and operable; no keyboard traps.
- Custom widgets (KNM tabs, exam UI) follow [ARIA APG patterns](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/).
- Do not remove `:focus-visible` without a visible replacement (≥ 3:1 contrast).
- One `<h1>` per page; no skipped heading levels.
- Landmarks: `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`; distinct `aria-label` on multiple navs.
- Skip link as first focusable element (`BaseLayout.astro`).
- Unique, meaningful `<title>` per route.

## Understandable

- Form inputs need associated `<label>`; placeholders are not labels.
- Errors linked with `aria-describedby`.
- Correct `lang` on `<html>` (set in `BaseLayout.astro` per locale).

## Robust

- Prefer native HTML over ARIA; use `<button>` not clickable `<div>`s.
- Dynamic updates (exam feedback, loading) use `aria-live` regions in KNM app.
- `aria-labelledby` / `aria-describedby` must reference existing ids.

## KNM app

- Text-node rendering for user-facing content — no `innerHTML`.
- Exam feedback announced via live regions.
- Large touch targets and readable type per PROJECT.md conventions.

## Legal copy

- Ask before editing legal wording in `src/i18n/legal.ts` or legal pages.
